<title>BELGIUM: EU vets Dutch packaging division sale.</title>
<headline>EU vets Dutch packaging division sale.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Friday it was opening a routine probe into a plan by U.S. company Tenneco to buy the protective and flexible packaging division of NV Koniklijke KNP BT.</p>
<p>Tenneco, which produces and sells packaging products and automotive exhaust and shock absorbtion systems, announced in March it had agreed to buy the division from the Dutch paper and packaging company for about $375 million.</p>
<p>The Commission said in a statement that the deal was submitted for clearance on March 24 under the EU's merger rules, which ban creation or strengthening of dominant positions.</p>
<p>It has about a month to approve the deal or start a full probe. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
